---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import Fill from '../components/Fill.astro';
import { OWNER } from '../config/legal';
---

<LegalPage
  title="About us"
  description="B2BRated is a business software comparison site run by an individual. Here is what we aim to do, how pages are checked and how the site is paid for."
  path="/about"
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    B2BRated is a business software comparison site run by an individual, <Fill value={OWNER.legalName} label="legal name" />,
    based in <Fill value={OWNER.country} label="country" />. Postal address for legal notices:
    <Fill value={OWNER.address} label="address" />. You can reach us at <Fill value={OWNER.email} label="contact email" />.
  </p>

  <h2>What we are trying to do</h2>
  <p>
    Our goal is to make business software pricing and features something a buyer can check for themselves. Every price on
    the site links to the vendor page it came from, so you can open the source and confirm the figure before you rely on
    it. The same goes for features: a claim about what a plan includes should be traceable to something the vendor has
    published, not to our say-so.
  </p>

  <h2>How a product earns a listing</h2>
  <p>
    Each category has a written capability list. A product is listed only when it meets that list, and we check each
    point against the vendor's own documentation. The <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a> sets out the details.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some vendors publish no price and only quote. We still list them when their own pages confirm the features, and we
    mark them quote only. A missing price is not a reason to leave a good product out, but we will not guess one either.
  </p>

  <h2>Who writes and checks the pages</h2>
  <p>
    Category pages are drafted with AI assistance and checked against vendors' own pages. They are then signed off by
    <Fill value={OWNER.editor} label="editor name" />, who approves the inclusion criteria and the copy. A sign-off does
    not mean the editor has used every product. It means the editor has read the criteria and the copy and agrees that
    they say what the vendors' pages support.
  </p>

  <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
  <p>
    Today the owner pays for the site and it earns nothing. No vendor pays us, and there are no affiliate links or ads.
    Later we may charge vendors for tools such as claimed profiles, lead requests and clearly labelled sponsored
    placements. Payment will never change a product's score or its place in the organic order. We will describe each paid
    product on the <a href="/advertising-disclosure">advertising and sponsorship page</a> before the first payment.
  </p>

  <h2>Reviews and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Reviews and user accounts are not open yet. When reviews open, only signed-in users can write them, and the
    <a href="/review-guidelines">review guidelines</a> apply.
  </p>
  <p>
    If something on a page is wrong, tell us on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> and include a link to a public
    page that shows the correct fact.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
